<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rohtak</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rohtak is a city in the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. Excavations at the nearby mound of Khokrakot have produced coin moulds of the Yaudheya republic, showing that the area was an important Yaudheya centre in the early centuries CE. It is today a district headquarters and an educational centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rohtak.jpg" alt="Rohtak" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mananjainhsr · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_Institute_of_Management_Rohtak,_Academic_Block.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
